PDHCG — Linux build, installation and verification
==================================================

Validated configuration: Ubuntu 22.04.5 x86_64, GCC/G++ 11.4.0,
CMake 3.30.5, Python 3.10.12, NumPy 1.26.4.
C/C++ compiler, CMake >=3.24, CUDA Toolkit, NVIDIA GPU/driver, zlib development headers, Python 3 and NumPy. PreFOS, MPI/NCCL and Python bindings are disabled.

1. Install compiler/build tools and the listed system development dependencies.
   On Ubuntu the common packages are build-essential and python3-pip.
   For this project also install zlib1g-dev.
   No sudo command is executed by this package's build.sh.

2. From the package root, install private test/build tooling if needed:
   python3 -m pip install --target "$PWD/.coinor-deps/python" numpy==1.26.4 cmake==3.30.5
   export PYTHONPATH="$PWD/.coinor-deps/python${PYTHONPATH:+:$PYTHONPATH}"
   export CMAKE="$PWD/.coinor-deps/python/cmake/data/bin/cmake"

3. For GPU execution, install NVIDIA drivers and a Linux CUDA Toolkit.
   Tested: RTX 4090, driver 580.82.07, Toolkit 12.8.93.
   export CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-12.8
   export CUDACXX="$CUDA_HOME/bin/nvcc"
   export PATH="$CUDA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
   export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
   export GPU_ARCH=89
   GPU_ARCH defaults to native; use 89 for RTX 4090 or 90 for H100.

4. Run: bash build.sh
   Installed CLI: .coinor-deps/pdhcg-install/bin/pdhcg
   The numerical test uses this installed executable, not the build-tree copy.
   The checker regression additionally rejects old results and wrong fresh solutions.

All build/test commands return nonzero on failure. Numerical reports under
tests/logs/ contain pass=true on success, with per-invocation raw output folders.
The negative checker regression deliberately induces failures and succeeds only
when those failures are detected. Do not count its induced solver failures as
successful solves. See tests/README.md for expected answers and adding tests.
The documented build does not fetch PreFOS or other source dependencies.
Installing external tooling and dependencies may require network access.
Only source is shipped. Optional interfaces are documented in README.md.
